      "Continuing Education and Coming Back",
      "Many states follow NASAA's continuing education (CE) rule for IARs. It has two parts:\n• Ethics and Professional Responsibility: the IAR's ethical and legal duties\n• Products and Practice: investment products and industry practices\nIARs must finish six credits in each part by the end of each calendar year.\n\nAn IAR who misses CE renews as \"CE Inactive\" until it is done. An IAR still CE Inactive at the end of the next year cannot renew. An IAR who leaves and wants to come back must make up all missed CE or retake the Series 65 or 66. IARs who are also FINRA-registered agents meet CE by completing FINRA's yearly regulatory and firm elements.\n\nPeople who leave the industry lose their registration. If they come back within two years, they can resume without retaking their exams. NASAA's Exam Validity Extension Program (EVEP) can stretch that to five years. To qualify, a person must:\n• Have been registered at least one year before leaving\n• Elect EVEP within two years of leaving\n• Take part in FINRA's Maintaining Qualifications Program (MQP), which requires yearly CE\nSomeone who joins within the two years must make up any CE they missed.",
