      "Investment companies include UITs, closed-end funds, mutual funds, and face-amount certificates. When discussing them, professionals:\n• Must disclose all sales charges and discounts, like breakpoints, letters of intent, and rights of accumulation\n• Cannot call a fund \"no load\" or say \"no sales charge\" if it has a sales charge or a 12b-1 fee above 0.25%\n• Must make sure the share class recommended is suitable\n• Should not recommend buying or switching among several funds with the same objective\n• Must show average annual returns for 1, 5, and 10 years if they show current income\n• Must explain how a fund's risks differ from other investments they recommend\n• Cannot project future performance or make unwarranted claims\n• Cannot \"sell dividends,\" which means urging a client to buy just before a dividend is paid\n• Must describe all material facts and risks\n• Cannot mark up or highlight parts of the prospectus",
